// /types-of-personal-goals v2.4 page data (2026-11-06): v2.3.3 rewritten around Brandon's 2026-11-06 email and reference packet, to match /goal-setting v2.4:
// five life areas (faith, family, fitness, work, personal; the app's own pillars, Grant's call 2026-11-06), accomplishment vs commitment, commitment
// frequency separate from the group's reporting cycle, tracking optional, members choose their commitments after discussion, 8-12 week focus as an
// option, a "what would it take" check with deferring as a valid choice, faith examples framed as chosen practices, and an open-goal example with no target.
// Layout is the signed-off v2.3 template. Element changes: the family module is a commitment table (was the week calendar), 4.9 prose became a checklist,
// 4.7 is the "three clocks" stack, the work module has no photo (beats would stack up). Change list: docs/marketing/types-of-personal-goals-pillar-revision-2026-11-06.md
const GRID=[['Faith','Read three pages of the Bible each day','Finish a 90-day Gospel devotional by Easter','Try two ways to keep a daily quiet time','Count the mornings I journal with scripture this month'],['Family','Two dates with my spouse each month','Take a week-long family road trip this summer','Learn three ways to plan a trip on a budget','Count the evenings the phone stays off this month'],['Fitness','Three strength sessions a week','Finish a marathon in the fall','Learn three strength lifts with good form','Record every run this month and see how far I get'],['Work','One protected hour a week on a business idea','Ship one project this quarter','Learn to build a monthly budget','Count the prospect calls I make this month'],['Personal','Call a friend or family member each week','Hold a ten-minute conversation in Spanish by March','Try three ways to practice piano','Count the books I finish this year']];
